From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: playportdev <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:29:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32: hand every process of a session the whole root list

crypt32's unix side reads the trusted roots once, from MADEIRA_CA_BUNDLE,
and hands them to the PE side's sync_trusted_roots_from_known_locations
one by one, freeing each as it goes: upstream loads the unix side once per
Wine process, so one pass is all a list ever serves. Here it is loaded once
per app process and every Wine process of the session shares it, so only
the first process to open the ROOT store got the roots. A later one (the
title after a launcher, a crash handler) found the list empty, and since
the roots it had imported were recorded under HostImportedCertificates,
its sync deleted every one of them from the prefix's ROOT store.

The list is now kept and walked: the enumeration returns its entries in
order and STATUS_NO_MORE_ENTRIES at its end, then starts again from the
head for the next process. The PE side serialises the processes' syncs
with its crypt32_root_semaphore, so two walks do not interleave.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-07-guest-tls-roots.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/crypto-unix/crypt32_unixlib_ios.c | 26 +++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/crypto-unix/crypt32_unixlib_ios.c b/build/crypto-unix/crypt32_unixlib_ios.c
index 073a3e9..cb563df 100644
--- a/build/crypto-unix/crypt32_unixlib_ios.c
+++ b/build/crypto-unix/crypt32_unixlib_ios.c
@@ -1016,24 +1016,38 @@ static void load_root_certs(void)
         import_certs_from_path( CRYPT_knownLocations[i], TRUE );
 }
 
+/* Playport: this unix side is loaded once per app process and shared by every
+ * Wine process of its session (the session root, the title, the title's own
+ * children), where upstream loads it once per Wine process. Each process's
+ * crypt32 enumerates the list once (rootstore.c, serialised across processes
+ * by crypt32_root_semaphore), and a process that found it already consumed
+ * would delete every imported root from the registry. So the list is walked,
+ * not consumed, and the walk starts over after its end. */
 static NTSTATUS enum_root_certs( void *args )
 {
     struct enum_root_certs_params *params = args;
     static BOOL loaded;
-    struct list *ptr;
+    static struct list *next;
     struct root_cert *cert;
 
-    if (!loaded) load_root_certs();
+    if (!loaded)
+    {
+        load_root_certs();
+        next = list_head( &root_cert_list );
+    }
     loaded = TRUE;
 
-    if (!(ptr = list_head( &root_cert_list ))) return STATUS_NO_MORE_ENTRIES;
-    cert = LIST_ENTRY( ptr, struct root_cert, entry );
+    if (!next)
+    {
+        next = list_head( &root_cert_list );
+        return STATUS_NO_MORE_ENTRIES;
+    }
+    cert = LIST_ENTRY( next, struct root_cert, entry );
     *params->needed = cert->size;
     if (cert->size <= params->size)
     {
         memcpy( params->buffer, cert->data, cert->size );
-        list_remove( &cert->entry );
-        free( cert );
+        next = list_next( &root_cert_list, next );
     }
     return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
